---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Carrier Lookup API"
description: "Retrieve supported carrier identifiers and network-routing context for North American phone numbers. Enrich records, investigate data quality, and support fraud and telecom analysis."
---
{%- from "partials/macros.njk" import arrow, dot %}

<section class="page-hero page-hero--crumbs" aria-labelledby="page-title">
	<div class="wrap">
		{%- set crumbs = [{ label: "Products", href: "/products/" }] %}
		{%- set crumbCurrent = "Carrier Lookup" %}
		{%- include "partials/crumbs.njk" %}
		<div class="pair page-hero__grid">
			<div class="pair__copy pair__copy--wide">
				<p class="label label--ink label--dot">{{ dot() }}Carrier Lookup API</p>
				<h1 id="page-title" class="h1">Find the network behind the number.</h1>
				<p class="lede--hero">Enrich existing phone records with carrier-related information and routing context.</p>
				<p class="text">Understand more about the network associated with a phone number without maintaining your own telecommunications lookup infrastructure.</p>
				<div class="actions actions--mt">
					<a class="btn btn--ink" href="/contact/">Get API Access</a>
					<a class="btn btn--line" href="/developers/">View Documentation</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<figure class="pair__visual">
				<div class="panel">
					<div class="panel__head">
						<p class="panel__title">Carrier Lookup</p>
						<p class="label">Illustrative</p>
					</div>
					<div class="panel__body">
						<div class="trace trace--input">
							<div class="trace__rail" aria-hidden="true"></div>
							<div class="trace__content">
								<p class="label">Input</p>
								<p class="trace__input trace__input--sm">+1 212 555 0123</p>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="trace">
							<div class="trace__rail" aria-hidden="true"></div>
							<div class="trace__content">
								<div class="trace__field">
									<p class="trace__name">Carrier identifier</p>
									<p class="trace__key">carrier.ocn</p>
								</div>
								<p class="trace__value">9101</p>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="trace">
							<div class="trace__rail" aria-hidden="true"></div>
							<div class="trace__content">
								<div class="trace__field">
									<p class="trace__name">Location Routing Number</p>
									<p class="trace__key">routing.lrn</p>
								</div>
								<p class="trace__value">12125550000</p>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="trace trace--last">
							<div class="trace__rail" aria-hidden="true"></div>
							<div class="trace__content">
								<div class="trace__field">
									<p class="trace__name">Routing context</p>
									<p class="trace__key">routing.state · routing.lata</p>
								</div>
								<p class="trace__value">NY · 132</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				<figcaption class="caption">Illustrative response. Available identifiers vary by number.</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--line" aria-labelledby="does-title">
	<div class="wrap split">
		<p class="label split__label">What it does</p>
		<div class="split__body">
			<h2 id="does-title" class="h2">The telecommunications context behind your numbers.</h2>
			<div class="grid grid--250 grid--gap-md mt-md">
				<p class="text-md">Carrier Lookup retrieves supported carrier and network-routing information for North American telephone numbers.</p>
				<p class="text-md">It helps applications understand the telecommunications context behind numbers already present in their systems.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--line section--mist" aria-labelledby="use-title">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="split">
			<p class="label split__label">Use cases</p>
			<h2 id="use-title" class="h2 split__body">Put carrier data to work.</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="grid mt-lg">
			<div class="card">
				<p class="card__num">01</p>
				<h3 class="card__title">CRM enrichment</h3>
				<p class="card__text">Add carrier-related fields to existing contact records.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<p class="card__num">02</p>
				<h3 class="card__title">Data quality</h3>
				<p class="card__text">Investigate records where stored carrier information may be outdated.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<p class="card__num">03</p>
				<h3 class="card__title">Fraud investigations</h3>
				<p class="card__text">Compare network information with other customer and transaction signals.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<p class="card__num">04</p>
				<h3 class="card__title">Telecommunications analysis</h3>
				<p class="card__text">Use carrier and routing identifiers in network research and operational workflows.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--line" aria-labelledby="get-title">
	<div class="wrap split">
		<p class="label split__label">What you get</p>
		<div class="split__body">
			<h2 id="get-title" class="h2">Supported carrier-related identifiers and network-routing context.</h2>
			<p class="text-md mt-md">Available fields may include the following, depending on the product configuration:</p>
			<ul class="returns">
				<li class="returns__item returns__item--split"><span class="returns__name">{{ dot("dot--9") }}Originating carrier identifiers</span><span class="returns__code">carrier</span></li>
				<li class="returns__item returns__item--split"><span class="returns__name">{{ dot("dot--9") }}LRN-related information</span><span class="returns__code">routing.lrn</span></li>
				<li class="returns__item returns__item--split"><span class="returns__name">{{ dot("dot--9") }}Geographic routing attributes</span><span class="returns__code">routing.state · routing.lata</span></li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--line" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
	<div class="wrap split">
		<p class="label split__label">FAQ</p>
		<div class="split__body">
			<h2 id="faq-title" class="h2">Common questions.</h2>
			<dl class="faq">
				<div class="faq__item">
					<dt class="faq__q">Can a phone number change carriers?</dt>
					<dd class="faq__a">Yes. Number portability allows phone numbers to move between participating carriers.</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="faq__item">
					<dt class="faq__q">Does Carrier Lookup tell me whether a number is mobile?</dt>
					<dd class="faq__a">No. Carrier Lookup does not classify numbers as mobile, landline, or VoIP.</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="faq__item">
					<dt class="faq__q">Does Carrier Lookup confirm the number is active?</dt>
					<dd class="faq__a">No. It describes the network context of a number, not whether the number is in service.</dd>
				</div>
			</dl>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

{%- set related = ["enrich", "cnam", "lrn"] %}
{%- include "partials/related.njk" %}

{%- set cta = {
	title: "Understand more about the numbers in your data.",
	text: "Start with xGO Carrier Lookup.",
	primary: { label: "Get API Access", href: "/contact/" },
	secondary: { label: "View Documentation", href: "/developers/" }
} %}
{%- include "partials/cta-card.njk" %}
